          "Deep Pressure : Firm pressure is applied to release tight areas and knots (also known as adhesions) in the muscles.",
          "Friction : The therapist may use friction techniques to address specific muscle problems, such as adhesions or scar tissue.",
          "Stripping : This technique involves deep, gliding pressure along the length of the muscle fibers to realign tissue fibers and release tension.",
          "Trigger Point Therapy : Direct pressure is applied to specific points of tension or pain (trigger points) to alleviate discomfort and improve range of motion."
