          "I was excited to try this after a particularly grueling week of gym workouts and long runs. The sports massage was more functional, with the therapist focusing on the areas most affected by physical exertion, like my legs, calves, and shoulders. The techniques used involved stretching, joint manipulation, and targeted muscle work. It wasn’t as relaxing as some of the other massages I had experienced, but I could feel its benefits immediately. My muscles felt looser, and I noticed that I was less sore in the days following.",
